STEP 2 — Heap was proven committable before use, at the value used
====================================================================================================
The plan's test is commitment rather than reservation: -Xms and -Xmx equal, with +AlwaysPreTouch,
exiting zero. Reservation alone would not distinguish a host that can commit the heap from one
that cannot, and a heap that cannot be committed is how a truncated graph gets built quietly.

Proof taken before the invocation, verbatim from harness scratch (frontend-run/heap-commit-proof.txt):
