    How that figure was arrived at, stated because the raw sampler was faulty and a corrected
    number with no explanation would not be checkable:
      raw sampled peak  149,494,572 kB — DOUBLE-COUNTED, not used
      wrapper peak      2,084 kB, from the in-script sampler
      JVM peak          74,746,244 kB (71.3 GiB) = (raw - wrapper) / 2
      wrapper + JVM     74,748,328 kB (71.3 GiB)
      why the raw figure is wrong: The sampler iterated `for p in $(pgrep -P $WPID) $WPID` and, for each p, also added every child of p. When p reached $WPID itself the inner loop re-added the single JVM child, so the JVM's RSS entered the sum twice at every sample. The bug is uniform across all samples, so the peak of the raw series equals 2*JVM_peak + wrapper.
