W7 — the provenance limitation applies here too
    Per-entry provenance for overwritten entries is not measurable from this frontend's output,
    for the reason STEP 11 gives. No winner map is claimed for this graph either.

    But one collision's OUTCOME is measurable from the graph's own content, which is the route
    AAP 0.5.1 sanctions, and it is worth recording because it is substantive. In THIS graph the
    eleven classes sql/connect/shims ships as client-only stubs all carry stub-sized method
    counts (2 to 8 methods each), where the same classes in the graph at the sanctioned path -
    built from an input set that EXCLUDED the shims archives - carry a full implementation's
    worth (SparkConf 298, SparkContext 1,100, rdd.RDD 1,022, api.java.JavaRDD 74). So in a graph
    that contains the shims artifact, the stub definitions displaced the real ones for those
    eleven classes. Both sides of that comparison are published with their counts, each by the
    file that measured it: the stub-sized side, in THIS graph, in cpg-verify.log PART 2 STEP P5;
    the full-implementation side, in the graph at the sanctioned path, in
    harness/artifacts/logs/cpg-shims-collision-measurement.log, which queried that graph
    first-hand. It is NOT a winner map: it says what is in the graph, not
    which archive the frontend read last. It does corroborate the provisioning runbook's own
    instruction to exclude the shims archive, and it is a real cost of the complete input set
    the AAP mandates - recorded, not acted on, because the AAP forbids the exclusion.

W8 — what PART 2 does and does not establish
    Establishes: whether this frontend, from a module's own primary artifact, produces that
    module's witness into a loadable graph. cpg-verify.log PART 2 runs those 38 queries — one
    per JAR-producing module — against this graph, and STEP P4 there carries their results.
    Does not establish: coverage of the graph at harness/cpg/spark.cpg, which is a different
    graph over a different input set; and does not satisfy D1, which requires the mandated
    complete-input graph. A witness present in THIS graph is therefore never counted as a
    coverage verdict for the graph the runners read: those verdicts are in
    harness/artifacts/logs/cpg-module-coverage.json and cpg-verify.log PHASE 2, and 12 of the
    38 JAR-producing projects have no COVERED verdict there for the reasons that file names.

